IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `clpq-dates`

-- Choice of Law (Limitation Periods) Act 1996 (Queensland) -- the whole Act, as the CLAIMANT meets it.
--
-- SEAT: the person who brings a claim (for example for an injury suffered in another State, a Territory or New Zealand)
-- before a court or an arbitrator in Queensland, where the law of that other place governs the claim. "Is this time
-- limit a limitation law?", "Does the Act reach my proceeding?", "Whose limitation law will the court apply to my
-- claim?", "How will the court use a power to extend time under that law?", "Am I in time, and by when must I start?".
-- The person who answers the claim meets the same rules from the other side (NOTES.md, Seat); the court, the arbitrator
-- and the courts of the other place get no seat.
--
-- The Act is seven sections. It is a gate in front of a limitation period: it decides WHOSE limitation law applies, not
-- what that law says. The other place's limitation law is not deposited; its period, the day it runs from and whether
-- it gives a discretion to extend are asked as facts. Which place's substantive law governs the claim is decided by the
-- court under the rules of choice of law, which are outside this Act: it is asked as a fact. Whether a regulation has
-- declared that the Act applies to New Zealand (s 3(2)) is not deposited: it is asked. Whether a court extends time is
-- the court's judgment: it is asked, never decided.
--
-- Every exported question takes plain facts (yes/no, dates, numbers, a choice from a list). The limitation period is a
-- DEONTIC rule run inside; no question takes a DEONTIC or an EVENT.
--
-- Unofficial version. Based on content from the Queensland Legislation website at 6 November 2026. (c) The State of
-- Queensland, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Choice of Law (Limitation Periods) Act 1996: the claimant's questions`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `The facts the Act turns on`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 4 "court includes arbitrator". s 5 and s 6 speak of "a court of the State": with the definition, a Queensland court
-- or an arbitrator in Queensland (fork F1).
DECLARE `Where my claim is heard` IS ONE OF
    `a court of Queensland`
    `an arbitrator, in an arbitration in Queensland`
    `a court or an arbitrator outside Queensland`

-- s 4 "relevant place means another State, a Territory or New Zealand." "State" and "Territory" are not defined in the
-- Act (borrowed: asked by choice; fork F2). Queensland itself is not a relevant place. A "means" definition.
DECLARE `Place` IS ONE OF
    `Queensland`
    `another Australian State (New South Wales, Victoria, South Australia, Tasmania or Western Australia)`
    `an Australian Territory (for example the Australian Capital Territory or the Northern Territory)`
    `New Zealand`
    `a country other than Australia or New Zealand`

GIVEN `the place` IS A `Place`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4 -- a relevant place` `the place` IF
    CONSIDER `the place`
    WHEN `another Australian State (New South Wales, Victoria, South Australia, Tasmania or Western Australia)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an Australian Territory (for example the Australian Capital Territory or the Northern Territory)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `New Zealand` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `where heard` IS A `Where my claim is heard`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 4, 5, 6 -- a court of the State` `where heard` IF
    CONSIDER `where heard`
    WHEN `a court of Queensland` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an arbitrator, in an arbitration in Queensland` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 4 -- what a limitation law is`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 4 "limitation law means a law that provides for the limitation or exclusion of any liability or the barring of a
-- right of action for a claim by reference to the time when a proceeding on, or the arbitration of, the claim is
-- started." A "means" definition: JUST TRUE when both limbs hold, JUST FALSE otherwise.
GIVEN `it limits or excludes a liability or bars a right of action for a claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it does so by the time a proceeding or arbitration is started` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4 -- a limitation law` `it limits or excludes a liability or bars a right of action for a claim` `it does so by the time a proceeding or arbitration is started` MEANS
    IF `it limits or excludes a liability or bars a right of action for a claim` AND `it does so by the time a proceeding or arbitration is started`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

@export Is the time limit I face a "limitation law" under the Choice of Law (Limitation Periods) Act 1996 (Queensland) s 4? A limitation law is a law that limits or excludes a liability, or bars a right of action, for a claim by reference to the time when a proceeding on the claim (or its arbitration) is started. A time limit for something else, such as giving notice of a claim or lodging a claim form, is not one unless it works by the time a proceeding is started.
GIVEN `limits excludes or bars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law limits or excludes a liability, or bars a right of action, for your claim (for example it says no action may be brought, or the liability ends)
      `by the time proceedings start` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it does so by reference to the time when a court proceeding, or an arbitration, on your claim is started (for example "an action may not be brought after 3 years"), rather than by reference to some other step
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is this a limitation law` MEANS
    `s 4 -- a limitation law` `limits excludes or bars` `by the time proceedings start`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 2, 3 -- whether the Act reaches my proceeding`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 2 "This Act commences on a day to be fixed by proclamation." The proclamation is not deposited; the deposited
-- version is "in force from 1996-11-01", taken as the commencement (fork F3).
`the day this Act commenced` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 11 1996

-- s 3(1) "This Act applies to a cause of action that arose before the commencement of this Act but does not apply to a
-- proceeding started before the commencement." A flat negative: JUST FALSE kind for a proceeding started before
-- 1 November 1996. One started on that day is not started "before" it (fork F4).
GIVEN `the day started` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3(1) -- started before the commencement` `the day started` IF
    `the day` `the day started` `is before` `the day this Act commenced`

-- s 3(2) "This Act does not apply to New Zealand until it is declared under a regulation to apply."
-- s 3(3) "If-- (a) the substantive law of New Zealand is to govern a claim before a court of the State; and (b) a
-- proceeding on the claim is started before the declaration takes effect; this Act does not apply to the proceeding."
-- Whether a declaration has been made, and the day it takes effect, are asked (no regulation is deposited; fork F5).
-- "Until" is a period the text fixes: JUST FALSE kind while no declaration has effect.
DECLARE `New Zealand under s 3` IS ONE OF
    `the Act applies to New Zealand law for my proceeding`
    `the Act does not apply to New Zealand: no regulation has declared that it applies (s 3(2))`
    `the Act does not apply to my proceeding: it was started before the declaration for New Zealand took effect (s 3(3))`

GIVEN `a declaration has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it takes effect` IS A DATE
      `the day started` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `New Zealand under s 3`
`ss 3(2), 3(3) -- New Zealand` `a declaration has been made` `the day it takes effect` `the day started` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`a declaration has been made`)
        THEN `the Act does not apply to New Zealand: no regulation has declared that it applies (s 3(2))`
        IF `the day` `the day started` `is before` `the day it takes effect`
        THEN `the Act does not apply to my proceeding: it was started before the declaration for New Zealand took effect (s 3(3))`
        OTHERWISE `the Act applies to New Zealand law for my proceeding`

GIVEN `a declaration has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it takes effect` IS A DATE
      `the day started` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 3(2), 3(3) -- the Act reaches New Zealand law for my proceeding` `a declaration has been made` `the day it takes effect` `the day started` IF
    `ss 3(2), 3(3) -- New Zealand` `a declaration has been made` `the day it takes effect` `the day started` EQUALS `the Act applies to New Zealand law for my proceeding`

DECLARE `Does the Act reach my proceeding` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the Act applies to my proceeding; my cause of action arose on or after 1 November 1996`
    `yes: the Act applies to my proceeding; my cause of action arose before 1 November 1996, and s 3(1) applies the Act to it`
    `no: the Act does not apply to a proceeding started before 1 November 1996 (s 3(1))`
    `no: New Zealand law governs my claim, and no regulation has declared that the Act applies to New Zealand (s 3(2))`
    `no: New Zealand law governs my claim, and my proceeding was started before the declaration for New Zealand took effect (s 3(3))`

GIVEN `the day the cause arose` IS A DATE
      `the day started` IS A DATE
      `the governing place` IS A `Place`
      `a declaration has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it takes effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Does the Act reach my proceeding`
`s 3 -- the Act reaches my proceeding` `the day the cause arose` `the day started` `the governing place` `a declaration has been made` `the day it takes effect` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 3(1) -- started before the commencement` `the day started`
        THEN `no: the Act does not apply to a proceeding started before 1 November 1996 (s 3(1))`
        IF (`the governing place` EQUALS `New Zealand`) AND (NOT (`a declaration has been made`))
        THEN `no: New Zealand law governs my claim, and no regulation has declared that the Act applies to New Zealand (s 3(2))`
        IF (`the governing place` EQUALS `New Zealand`) AND (NOT (`ss 3(2), 3(3) -- the Act reaches New Zealand law for my proceeding` `a declaration has been made` `the day it takes effect` `the day started`))
        THEN `no: New Zealand law governs my claim, and my proceeding was started before the declaration for New Zealand took effect (s 3(3))`
        IF `the day` `the day the cause arose` `is before` `the day this Act commenced`
        THEN `yes: the Act applies to my proceeding; my cause of action arose before 1 November 1996, and s 3(1) applies the Act to it`
        OTHERWISE `yes: the Act applies to my proceeding; my cause of action arose on or after 1 November 1996`

@export Does the Choice of Law (Limitation Periods) Act 1996 (Queensland) reach my proceeding (ss 2, 3)? The Act commenced on 1 November 1996. It applies to a cause of action that arose before that day, but not to a proceeding started before that day. It does not apply to New Zealand until a regulation declares that it does, and not to a proceeding governed by New Zealand law that was started before that declaration took effect.
GIVEN `day cause arose` IS A DATE @desc The day your cause of action arose (for example the day you were injured), as an ISO date such as 2025-03-14
      `day started` IS A DATE @desc The day your court proceeding was, or will be, started (or your arbitration begun), as an ISO date
      `governing place` IS A `Place` @desc The place whose substantive law governs your claim, as the court decides under the rules of choice of law: Queensland; another Australian State; an Australian Territory; New Zealand; or a country other than Australia or New Zealand
      `NZ declared` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a Queensland regulation has declared that this Act applies to New Zealand (s 3(2)); matters only if New Zealand law governs your claim
      `NZ declaration day` IS A DATE @desc If such a declaration has been made, the day it takes effect, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
GIVETH A `Does the Act reach my proceeding`
`Does the Act reach my proceeding` MEANS
    `s 3 -- the Act reaches my proceeding` `day cause arose` `day started` `governing place` `NZ declared` `NZ declaration day`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 5 -- whose limitation law the court applies`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 5 "If the substantive law of a relevant place is to govern a claim before a court of the State, a limitation law of
-- the relevant place is to be regarded as part of that substantive law and applied accordingly by the court."
-- "If": when a limb fails, s 5 does not apply (JUST FALSE kind). Which limitation law then applies is outside the Act
-- (fork F9). Which place's substantive law governs the claim is the court's choice-of-law decision: asked.
DECLARE `The limitation law the court applies` IS ONE OF
    `that place's limitation law, as part of the substantive law that governs my claim (s 5)`
    `s 5 does not apply: my claim is not before a court or an arbitrator of Queensland`
    `s 5 does not apply: my proceeding was started before 1 November 1996 (s 3(1))`
    `s 5 does not apply: no regulation has declared that the Act applies to New Zealand (s 3(2))`
    `s 5 does not apply: my proceeding was started before the declaration for New Zealand took effect (s 3(3))`
    `s 5 does not apply: Queensland law governs my claim; Queensland's own limitation law is outside this Act`
    `s 5 does not apply: the law of a country other than New Zealand governs my claim; which limitation law applies is outside this Act`

GIVEN `where heard` IS A `Where my claim is heard`
      `the governing place` IS A `Place`
      `the day started` IS A DATE
      `a declaration has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it takes effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `The limitation law the court applies`
`s 5 -- the limitation law the court applies` `where heard` `the governing place` `the day started` `a declaration has been made` `the day it takes effect` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`ss 4, 5, 6 -- a court of the State` `where heard`)
        THEN `s 5 does not apply: my claim is not before a court or an arbitrator of Queensland`
        IF `s 3(1) -- started before the commencement` `the day started`
        THEN `s 5 does not apply: my proceeding was started before 1 November 1996 (s 3(1))`
        IF (`the governing place` EQUALS `New Zealand`) AND (NOT (`a declaration has been made`))
        THEN `s 5 does not apply: no regulation has declared that the Act applies to New Zealand (s 3(2))`
        IF (`the governing place` EQUALS `New Zealand`) AND (NOT (`ss 3(2), 3(3) -- the Act reaches New Zealand law for my proceeding` `a declaration has been made` `the day it takes effect` `the day started`))
        THEN `s 5 does not apply: my proceeding was started before the declaration for New Zealand took effect (s 3(3))`
        IF `s 4 -- a relevant place` `the governing place`
        THEN `that place's limitation law, as part of the substantive law that governs my claim (s 5)`
        IF `the governing place` EQUALS `Queensland`
        THEN `s 5 does not apply: Queensland law governs my claim; Queensland's own limitation law is outside this Act`
        OTHERWISE `s 5 does not apply: the law of a country other than New Zealand governs my claim; which limitation law applies is outside this Act`

GIVEN `where heard` IS A `Where my claim is heard`
      `the governing place` IS A `Place`
      `the day started` IS A DATE
      `a declaration has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it takes effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5 applies` `where heard` `the governing place` `the day started` `a declaration has been made` `the day it takes effect` IF
    `s 5 -- the limitation law the court applies` `where heard` `the governing place` `the day started` `a declaration has been made` `the day it takes effect` EQUALS `that place's limitation law, as part of the substantive law that governs my claim (s 5)`

@export Whose limitation law will the Queensland court (or arbitrator) apply to my claim (Choice of Law (Limitation Periods) Act 1996 (Queensland) s 5)? If the substantive law of another State, a Territory or New Zealand governs your claim before a court or arbitrator in Queensland, that place's limitation law counts as part of its substantive law and the court applies it, not Queensland's. New Zealand counts only once a regulation declares that the Act applies to it. Which place's law governs your claim is for the court under the rules of choice of law, which this Act does not decide.
GIVEN `where heard` IS A `Where my claim is heard` @desc Where your claim is heard: a court of Queensland; an arbitrator, in an arbitration in Queensland; or a court or an arbitrator outside Queensland
      `governing place` IS A `Place` @desc The place whose substantive law governs your claim, as the court decides under the rules of choice of law: Queensland; another Australian State; an Australian Territory; New Zealand; or a country other than Australia or New Zealand
      `day started` IS A DATE @desc The day your proceeding was, or will be, started (or your arbitration begun), as an ISO date
      `NZ declared` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a Queensland regulation has declared that this Act applies to New Zealand (s 3(2)); matters only if New Zealand law governs your claim
      `NZ declaration day` IS A DATE @desc If such a declaration has been made, the day it takes effect, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
GIVETH A `The limitation law the court applies`
`Whose limitation law applies to my claim` MEANS
    `s 5 -- the limitation law the court applies` `where heard` `governing place` `day started` `NZ declared` `NZ declaration day`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 6 -- how a discretion under that limitation law is used`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 6 "If a court of the State exercises a discretion conferred under a limitation law of a relevant place, the
-- discretion, as far as practicable, is to be exercised in the way in which it is exercised in comparable cases by the
-- courts of the relevant place."
-- "If": when a limb fails, s 6 does not apply (JUST FALSE kind). Whether that law confers a discretion is that law's
-- (asked); how it comes out is the court's judgment (never decided). s 3 limits the whole Act, so s 6 too (fork F10).
DECLARE `How the discretion is exercised` IS ONE OF
    `as far as practicable, in the way in which the courts of that place exercise it in comparable cases (s 6)`
    `s 6 does not apply: the discretion is not exercised by a court or an arbitrator of Queensland`
    `s 6 does not apply: my proceeding was started before 1 November 1996 (s 3(1))`
    `s 6 does not apply: the limitation law is not one of a relevant place (another State, a Territory or New Zealand)`
    `s 6 does not apply: no regulation has declared that the Act applies to New Zealand (s 3(2))`
    `s 6 does not apply: my proceeding was started before the declaration for New Zealand took effect (s 3(3))`
    `s 6 does not apply: that place's limitation law confers no discretion in my case`

GIVEN `where heard` IS A `Where my claim is heard`
      `the place of the limitation law` IS A `Place`
      `that law confers a discretion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day started` IS A DATE
      `a declaration has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it takes effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `How the discretion is exercised`
`s 6 -- how the discretion is exercised` `where heard` `the place of the limitation law` `that law confers a discretion` `the day started` `a declaration has been made` `the day it takes effect` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`ss 4, 5, 6 -- a court of the State` `where heard`)
        THEN `s 6 does not apply: the discretion is not exercised by a court or an arbitrator of Queensland`
        IF `s 3(1) -- started before the commencement` `the day started`
        THEN `s 6 does not apply: my proceeding was started before 1 November 1996 (s 3(1))`
        IF NOT (`s 4 -- a relevant place` `the place of the limitation law`)
        THEN `s 6 does not apply: the limitation law is not one of a relevant place (another State, a Territory or New Zealand)`
        IF (`the place of the limitation law` EQUALS `New Zealand`) AND (NOT (`a declaration has been made`))
        THEN `s 6 does not apply: no regulation has declared that the Act applies to New Zealand (s 3(2))`
        IF (`the place of the limitation law` EQUALS `New Zealand`) AND (NOT (`ss 3(2), 3(3) -- the Act reaches New Zealand law for my proceeding` `a declaration has been made` `the day it takes effect` `the day started`))
        THEN `s 6 does not apply: my proceeding was started before the declaration for New Zealand took effect (s 3(3))`
        IF NOT (`that law confers a discretion`)
        THEN `s 6 does not apply: that place's limitation law confers no discretion in my case`
        OTHERWISE `as far as practicable, in the way in which the courts of that place exercise it in comparable cases (s 6)`

@export If the limitation law of another State, a Territory or New Zealand gives the court a discretion (for example to extend the time for starting my claim), how will the Queensland court use it (Choice of Law (Limitation Periods) Act 1996 (Queensland) s 6)? As far as practicable, the court exercises it in the way the courts of that place exercise it in comparable cases. Whether it will be exercised in your favour is for the court; this question does not decide it.
GIVEN `where heard` IS A `Where my claim is heard` @desc Where your claim is heard: a court of Queensland; an arbitrator, in an arbitration in Queensland; or a court or an arbitrator outside Queensland
      `place of the limitation law` IS A `Place` @desc The place whose limitation law gives the discretion: Queensland; another Australian State; an Australian Territory; New Zealand; or a country other than Australia or New Zealand
      `confers a discretion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that place's limitation law gives the court a discretion in your case (for example a power to extend the limitation period)
      `day started` IS A DATE @desc The day your proceeding was, or will be, started (or your arbitration begun), as an ISO date
      `NZ declared` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a Queensland regulation has declared that this Act applies to New Zealand (s 3(2)); matters only if the limitation law is New Zealand's
      `NZ declaration day` IS A DATE @desc If such a declaration has been made, the day it takes effect, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
GIVETH A `How the discretion is exercised`
`How will the court use a discretion under that law` MEANS
    `s 6 -- how the discretion is exercised` `where heard` `place of the limitation law` `confers a discretion` `day started` `NZ declared` `NZ declaration day`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 5, 6 -- am I in time under that place's limitation law`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- What s 5 means for the claimant: the period of the relevant place's limitation law is the one to meet. The period,
-- the day it runs from and any extension are that law's and that court's (asked). The last day is the same day of the
-- month the period's years and months after the day it runs from (fork F6; F7 for a day the month lacks); starting on
-- the last day is in time, the day after is not.
DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF `I`
DECLARE `Act done` IS ONE OF `start my proceeding or arbitration`

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act done`
`s 5 -- start within that place's limitation period` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `I`
    DO `start my proceeding or arbitration`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `I` BECAUSE "the proceeding was not started within the limitation period of the relevant place whose law governs the claim, which s 5 makes the Queensland court apply"

-- The helper that runs the rule over what happened. On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but
-- not BREACH. It takes a DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Party` `Act done`
      `the time it was done` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `started in time under` `the rule` `at` `the time it was done` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time it was done`), (EVENT `I` `start my proceeding or arbitration` `the time it was done`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Started on or before the last day? A proceeding started before the period begins to run is in time (fork F8).
GIVEN `the day the period runs from` IS A DATE, `the last day` IS A DATE, `the day started` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `started by the last day` `the day the period runs from` `the last day` `the day started` IF
    IF `the day` `the day started` `is before` `the day the period runs from`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE `started in time under` (`s 5 -- start within that place's limitation period` (`the days from` `the day the period runs from` `to` `the last day`)) `at` (`the days from` `the day the period runs from` `to` `the day started`)

DECLARE `Am I in time` IS ONE OF
    `not covered: s 5 does not make another place's limitation law apply to my claim (ask whose limitation law applies)`
    `yes, in time: I start within that place's limitation period, which the court applies (s 5)`
    `no, out of time under that place's limitation period (s 5), unless the court extends the time under a discretion that law gives, exercised as that place's courts would (s 6)`
    `yes, in time: the court has extended the time under that place's limitation law (s 6), and I start by the extended day`
    `no, out of time even as the court extended it under that place's limitation law (s 6)`

GIVEN `where heard` IS A `Where my claim is heard`
      `the governing place` IS A `Place`
      `a declaration has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it takes effect` IS A DATE
      `the years` IS A NUMBER
      `the months` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the period runs from` IS A DATE
      `the time was extended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the extended last day` IS A DATE
      `the day started` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Am I in time`
`ss 5, 6 -- am I in time` `where heard` `the governing place` `a declaration has been made` `the day it takes effect` `the years` `the months` `the day the period runs from` `the time was extended` `the extended last day` `the day started` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 5 applies` `where heard` `the governing place` `the day started` `a declaration has been made` `the day it takes effect`)
        THEN `not covered: s 5 does not make another place's limitation law apply to my claim (ask whose limitation law applies)`
        IF `the time was extended`
        THEN IF `started by the last day` `the day the period runs from` `the extended last day` `the day started`
             THEN `yes, in time: the court has extended the time under that place's limitation law (s 6), and I start by the extended day`
             ELSE `no, out of time even as the court extended it under that place's limitation law (s 6)`
        IF `started by the last day` `the day the period runs from` (`the date` `the years` `years and` `the months` `months after` `the day the period runs from`) `the day started`
        THEN `yes, in time: I start within that place's limitation period, which the court applies (s 5)`
        OTHERWISE `no, out of time under that place's limitation period (s 5), unless the court extends the time under a discretion that law gives, exercised as that place's courts would (s 6)`

@export Am I in time to start my claim in Queensland when another State's, a Territory's or New Zealand's law governs it (Choice of Law (Limitation Periods) Act 1996 (Queensland) ss 5, 6)? The court applies that place's limitation period, not Queensland's. Give the period that place's law sets for your claim and the day it runs from (both from that place's law, which this question does not hold), and say whether the court has extended the time under that law. Whether it will extend is for the court.
GIVEN `where heard` IS A `Where my claim is heard` @desc Where your claim is heard: a court of Queensland; an arbitrator, in an arbitration in Queensland; or a court or an arbitrator outside Queensland
      `governing place` IS A `Place` @desc The place whose substantive law governs your claim, as the court decides under the rules of choice of law: Queensland; another Australian State; an Australian Territory; New Zealand; or a country other than Australia or New Zealand
      `NZ declared` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a Queensland regulation has declared that this Act applies to New Zealand (s 3(2)); matters only if New Zealand law governs your claim
      `NZ declaration day` IS A DATE @desc If such a declaration has been made, the day it takes effect, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
      `period years` IS A NUMBER @desc The whole years in the limitation period that place's law sets for your claim (for example 3); 0 if the period is in months only
      `period months` IS A NUMBER @desc Any further whole months in that period (for example 0, or 6); 0 if none
      `period runs from` IS A DATE @desc The day that place's law says the period runs from (for example the day your cause of action arose, or the day you discovered it), as an ISO date
      `time extended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has extended the time for starting your claim under a discretion in that place's limitation law
      `extended last day` IS A DATE @desc If the time was extended, the last day the court allowed, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
      `day started` IS A DATE @desc The day your proceeding was, or will be, started (or your arbitration begun), as an ISO date
GIVETH A `Am I in time`
`Am I in time under that place's limitation law` MEANS
    `ss 5, 6 -- am I in time` `where heard` `governing place` `NZ declared` `NZ declaration day` `period years` `period months` `period runs from` `time extended` `extended last day` `day started`

-- The last day to start: the extended day if the court extended the time, otherwise the period counted from the day it
-- runs from. NOTHING where s 5 does not make another place's limitation law apply (the Act then sets no day).
GIVEN `where heard` IS A `Where my claim is heard`
      `the governing place` IS A `Place`
      `a declaration has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it takes effect` IS A DATE
      `the years` IS A NUMBER
      `the months` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the period runs from` IS A DATE
      `the time was extended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the extended last day` IS A DATE
      `the day started` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`ss 5, 6 -- the last day to start` `where heard` `the governing place` `a declaration has been made` `the day it takes effect` `the years` `the months` `the day the period runs from` `the time was extended` `the extended last day` `the day started` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 5 applies` `where heard` `the governing place` `the day started` `a declaration has been made` `the day it takes effect`)
        THEN NOTHING
        IF `the time was extended`
        THEN JUST `the extended last day`
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the date` `the years` `years and` `the months` `months after` `the day the period runs from`)

@export By when must I start my claim in Queensland when another State's, a Territory's or New Zealand's law governs it (Choice of Law (Limitation Periods) Act 1996 (Queensland) ss 5, 6)? The last day of that place's limitation period, counted from the day that law says it runs from; or the later day the court allowed, if it extended the time under that law. No answer if s 5 does not apply to your claim.
GIVEN `where heard` IS A `Where my claim is heard` @desc Where your claim is heard: a court of Queensland; an arbitrator, in an arbitration in Queensland; or a court or an arbitrator outside Queensland
      `governing place` IS A `Place` @desc The place whose substantive law governs your claim, as the court decides under the rules of choice of law: Queensland; another Australian State; an Australian Territory; New Zealand; or a country other than Australia or New Zealand
      `NZ declared` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a Queensland regulation has declared that this Act applies to New Zealand (s 3(2)); matters only if New Zealand law governs your claim
      `NZ declaration day` IS A DATE @desc If such a declaration has been made, the day it takes effect, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
      `period years` IS A NUMBER @desc The whole years in the limitation period that place's law sets for your claim (for example 3); 0 if the period is in months only
      `period months` IS A NUMBER @desc Any further whole months in that period (for example 0, or 6); 0 if none
      `period runs from` IS A DATE @desc The day that place's law says the period runs from (for example the day your cause of action arose, or the day you discovered it), as an ISO date
      `time extended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has extended the time for starting your claim under a discretion in that place's limitation law
      `extended last day` IS A DATE @desc If the time was extended, the last day the court allowed, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
      `day started` IS A DATE @desc The day your proceeding will be started (or your arbitration begun), as an ISO date; it decides whether s 3 lets the Act apply (not before 1 November 1996, and for New Zealand not before the declaration takes effect)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`By when must I start my claim` MEANS
    `ss 5, 6 -- the last day to start` `where heard` `governing place` `NZ declared` `NZ declaration day` `period years` `period months` `period runs from` `time extended` `extended last day` `day started`
